<div style="text-align:justify;margin-left:47.25pt;line-height:1.25;font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif">The
Company classifies cash equivalents within Level 1, and earnout is classified within Level 3, because the Company uses quoted market prices
or alternative pricing sources and models utilizing market observable inputs to determine their fair values.</span></span></div>

<div style="line-height:1.25">&#160;</div>

<div style="text-align:justify;margin-left:47.25pt;line-height:1.25;font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif">The
earnout was valued using a Monta Carlo simulation analysis, which is considered to be a Level 3 fair value measurement.</span></span></div>

<div style="text-align:justify;margin-left:47.25pt;line-height:1.25;font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif">&#160;</div>

